v3.2.18
Radon Player 3.2.18: True bit-perfect on Samsung
## 3.2.18: True bit-perfect on Samsung (Windows and Android)
- **True bit-perfect on Samsung and other phones:** Bit-perfect used Android's own bit-perfect mode, which only some phones have (Pixels do; Samsungs don't, for any DAC), so on those it was Android's mix, and it wrongly said your DAC didn't support it. Now, where Android has no bit-perfect mode, the app takes the USB DAC over and streams each song to it itself, the way USB Audio Player Pro does: at the song's own sample rate, its samples untouched (16-bit and 24-bit music exactly as in the file). Allow Radon Player to use the DAC once when Android asks (tick "always" when you plug it in and it isn't asked again). While it plays, the phone's volume buttons set the DAC's own volume, so the music stays bit-perfect at any volume, and other apps and notifications aren't heard through the DAC. Settings › Bit-perfect says what the DAC is getting. Turning bit-perfect off, unplugging the DAC or closing the app hands it back to Android.
- **Repeated lines tick on their own:** on a lyrics card, ticking a line that's sung more than once (a chorus line) ticked every copy of it and put it on the card only once. Each line now ticks on its own, so you can put the same line on the card twice.
- **Lyrics cards take up to 25 lines** (were 15). With more than 15 the card is taller (story-sized, 1080×1920) and the words get smaller as you tick more, so they always fit.
- **Crossfade no longer repeats the end of a song:** for the fade, a second player takes over the ending song while the next one comes in. It started a moment after it was told to, so it was a little behind, and at the handover you heard the last half second or so again (a word sung twice) before the fade began. It's now lined up to the exact spot you're hearing (silently, before it takes over), so the song just fades out where it is. If it can't be lined up in time, that one change happens without a fade rather than repeat anything.

### Good to know
- **Android:** install RadonPlayer.apk over 3.2.17 (same signature, your library and settings stay), or tap Update in Settings.
- **Windows:** Radon-Player-3.2.18.msi installs over 3.2.17, or use Update in Settings.
